# Terraform state and local working files.
#
# tfstate is the important one: Terraform records provider credentials,
# generated passwords and private keys in it as PLAINTEXT, regardless of whether
# the resource marked them sensitive. This repository is PUBLIC, so a committed
# state file is a disclosed state file.
#
# Flagged as at_risk by the nightly hygiene check on 2026-10-09 - untracked but
# also unignored, i.e. one `git add -A` away from being pushed.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Variable files routinely hold tokens and passwords. The .example stays
# committable as a template.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example

# Provider binaries and lock dirs - large, machine-specific, re-creatable.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Plan output can embed resolved secret values.
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
